  "identity": "Dutch-taught Dutch Language and Culture, 2026–2027. Separate from Dutch Studies for non-native speakers. OER articles 2.2, 2.3, 3.2.2 and 4.2 were inspected in indexed full text. The official programme overview and career pages were also inspected through indexed retrieval. Direct access blocks are recorded above.",
  "progression": "First-year required zero-credit mentoring. First year 30+30, then compulsory 30 EC in year-two autumn and 30 EC selected coursework in spring. The two required linguistics option courses and Critical Thinking, Critical Writing may be used in that spring. Year three uses open elective space in autumn and Recent Novels, Strategic Communication and the thesis in spring. First-year historical literature and Cognitive System 1 prerequisites are satisfied in the core, as is the humanities first-year requirement for Dutch Media and Society. The current Dutch Linguistics seminar requires prior specialisation coursework and is necessary for the 10 EC thesis. Choose a qualitative thesis project; quantitative projects additionally require Statistics for the Humanities I. The programme product lists the thesis in both semesters and specifies 10 EC for the combined group, with 0 EC assigned to the seminar.",
